       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum daily dose of 10 mg. At that dose the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged peripheral edema or shock. Normal kidney and liver function wouldn't offset that.\n\nDid you mean 5 mg once daily? That's a common starting dose, and 10 mg is the ceiling. A dropped or added zero is an easy mistake to make.\n\nTell me which of these you want:\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily\n- **50 mg** by mouth once daily, if it's intentional. I'd need you to confirm that, and I'd add a note with the rationale to the order.\n\nI'll enter it as soon as you confirm."
